L. J. Poppe, V. F. Paskevich, J. C. Hathaway, and D. S. Blackwood. A laboratory manual for X-ray powder diffraction. USGS Open-File Report 2001-41, 2001. DOI 10.3133/ofr0141. [Official publication, authors, and report route](https://www.usgs.gov/publications/a-laboratory-manual-x-ray-powder-diffraction).

Read the full manual for specimen preparation, diffraction, mineral identification, and the particular clay-fraction/treatment methods used in a study. Explain how preparation, preferred orientation, mixed layers, and treatment change the interpretation. Follow current laboratory procedures and instrument guidance for actual work, preserving the historical manual's edition.

Official authors, date, DOI, and report identity were checked on 29 October 2026. Free institutional source access is distinguished from a claim that every externally credited component is unrestricted. No powder patterns, laboratory media, or report PDF is bundled; selected primary-data references stay external.

